    "maintainer_can_modify": true,
    "title": "rpc: avoid quadratic `gettxspendingprevout` work and preserve order",
    "user": {
      "login": "l0rinc",
      "id": 1841944,
      "node_id": "MDQ6VXNlcjE4NDE5NDQ=",
      "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1841944?v=4",
      "gravatar_id": "",
      "url": "https://api.github.com/users/l0rinc",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/l0rinc",
      "followers_url": "https://api.github.com/users/l0rinc/followers",
      "following_url": "https://api.github.com/users/l0rinc/following%7B/other_user%7D",
      "gists_url": "https://api.github.com/users/l0rinc/gists%7B/gist_id%7D",
      "starred_url": "https://api.github.com/users/l0rinc/starred%7B/owner%7D%7B/repo%7D",
      "subscriptions_url": "https://api.github.com/users/l0rinc/subscriptions",
      "organizations_url": "https://api.github.com/users/l0rinc/orgs",
      "repos_url": "https://api.github.com/users/l0rinc/repos",
      "events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/l0rinc/events%7B/privacy%7D",
      "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/l0rinc/received_events",
      "type": "User",
      "site_admin": false,
      "name": null,
      "patch_url": null
    },
    "body": "Problem: `gettxspendingprevout` erases each mempool result from a vector while holding `mempool.cs`.\r\nEach erase moves the remaining requests, so a large RPC call does quadratic work in the mempool critical section.\r\nAn [operation-count model](https://godbolt.org/z/KKfsdT3fr) shows nearly 50 million moves for 10,000 mempool matches.\r\nMixed requests also return mempool results before txospender index results instead of preserving request order.\r\nBoth regressions were introduced by #34749.\r\n\r\nFix: Compact the mempool worklist once, store each result in its request position, and resolve only the remaining entries through the txospender index.\r\nThe mempool pass is linear and the response follows request order.\r\n\r\nReproducer: The [functional benchmark](https://gist.github.com/l0rinc/c3231e287cacfdefd100dbf95cd0c3ad) sends mempool-only requests with 8,000 through 128,000 entries ten times per size.\r\nUsing identical settings for the unfixed and fixed commits on each machine:\r\n\r\n```text\r\nAMD Ryzen 7 3700X (8 cores)\r\nunfixed  ██████████████████████████████  90 s\r\nfixed    ███▒░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░  10 s  (-80 s, 9.0x faster)\r\n\r\nRaspberry Pi 5 (4 cores)\r\nunfixed  ██████████████████████████████  685 s\r\nfixed    ▓░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░  22 s  (-663 s, 31.1x faster)\r\n```\r\n\r\nOn a Raspberry Pi 4 with 1 GB RAM, the unfixed run timed out after ~9 minutes.\r\n\r\n<details><summary>Benchmark command</summary>\r\n\r\n```bash\r\nfor commit in 963b061358b489b2ff4ff64895f2b895b3b89844 46e7173550a93cbe9d4e8ea28cfe7216286d8197; do \\\r\n  git fetch origin \"$commit\" && git checkout --detach \"$commit\" && \\\r\n  rm -rfd build && cmake -B build -G Ninja -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release -DBUILD_TESTS=OFF -DENABLE_WALLET=OFF >/dev/null 2>&1 && \\\r\n  ninja -C build -j1 bitcoind >/dev/null 2>&1 && \\\r\n  build/test/functional/test_runner.py rpc_gettxspendingprevout_quadratic.py --repeats=10 || break; \\\r\ndone\r\n```\r\n</details>\r\n",
