      "node_id": "C_kwDOABII59oAKDQ2ZTcxNzM1NTBhOTNjYmU5ZDRlOGVhMjhjZmU3MjE2Mjg2ZDgxOTc",
      "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/bitcoin/bitcoin/git/commits/46e7173550a93cbe9d4e8ea28cfe7216286d8197",
      "actor": null,
      "commit_id": null,
      "commit_url": null,
      "created_at": null,
      "html_url": "https://github.com/bitcoin/bitcoin/commit/46e7173550a93cbe9d4e8ea28cfe7216286d8197",
      "tree": {
        "sha": "b5c1a72d4009584773d68b6c7037907617b0b524",
        "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/bitcoin/bitcoin/git/trees/b5c1a72d4009584773d68b6c7037907617b0b524"
      },
      "verification": {
        "verified": true,
        "reason": "valid",
        "payload": "tree b5c1a72d4009584773d68b6c7037907617b0b524\nparent 21c198f8d83b263d2afddf3f26ce1ed9d1fd7960\nauthor Lőrinc <pap.lorinc@gmail.com> 1785826088 -0700\ncommitter Lőrinc <pap.lorinc@gmail.com> 1785883435 -0700\n\nrpc: avoid quadratic prevout resolution\n\n`gettxspendingprevout` erases each mempool-resolved request from a vector while holding `mempool.cs`.\nEach erase moves the remaining entries, making mixed requests quadratic.\n\nUse `std::erase_if` to compact the worklist once.\nThe mempool pass becomes linear and response assembly remains unchanged.\n\nA functional benchmark sends mempool-only requests with 8,000 through 128,000 entries ten times per size.\nUsing identical settings for the unfixed and fixed commits on each machine:\n\nAMD Ryzen 7 3700X (8 cores)\nunfixed  ██████████████████████████████  90 s\nfixed    ███▒░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░  10 s  (-80 s, 9.0x faster)\n\nRaspberry Pi 5\nunfixed  ██████████████████████████████  685 s\nfixed    ▓░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░  22 s  (-663 s, 31.1x faster)\n\nOn a Raspberry Pi 4 with 1 GB RAM, the unfixed run timed out after ~9 minutes.\n",
        "signature": "-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niJEEABYKADkWIQQiU97U54YbP0PlTVgnCd/LLYEwhwUCanJrKxsUgAAAAAAEAA5t\nYW51MiwyLjUrMS4xMiwwLDMACgkQJwnfyy2BMIeT/AD/UXV/Bk4XVqI9lBHlHQ+c\n2o1O+VZYctMkqfbyyr27x2EA/3ByxPnR9q3v+bCWJqXHtLSLz4SaGscYc5huOKzE\n+XUD\n=25z7\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----"
      },
      "parents": [
        {
          "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/bitcoin/bitcoin/git/commits/21c198f8d83b263d2afddf3f26ce1ed9d1fd7960",
          "sha": "21c198f8d83b263d2afddf3f26ce1ed9d1fd7960",
          "html_url": "https://github.com/bitcoin/bitcoin/commit/21c198f8d83b263d2afddf3f26ce1ed9d1fd7960"
        }
      ],
      "message": "rpc: avoid quadratic prevout resolution\n\n`gettxspendingprevout` erases each mempool-resolved request from a vector while holding `mempool.cs`.\nEach erase moves the remaining entries, making mixed requests quadratic.\n\nUse `std::erase_if` to compact the worklist once.\nThe mempool pass becomes linear and response assembly remains unchanged.\n\nA functional benchmark sends mempool-only requests with 8,000 through 128,000 entries ten times per size.\nUsing identical settings for the unfixed and fixed commits on each machine:\n\nAMD Ryzen 7 3700X (8 cores)\nunfixed  ██████████████████████████████  90 s\nfixed    ███▒░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░  10 s  (-80 s, 9.0x faster)\n\nRaspberry Pi 5\nunfixed  ██████████████████████████████  685 s\nfixed    ▓░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░  22 s  (-663 s, 31.1x faster)\n\nOn a Raspberry Pi 4 with 1 GB RAM, the unfixed run timed out after ~9 minutes.",
      "committer": {
        "name": "Lőrinc",
        "email": "pap.lorinc@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-08-04T22:43:55Z"
